# sent_id = tlg2046.tlg001.perseus-grc2.1.7
# text = τὴν γάρ ῥα κατέκτανε δουρὶ κραταιῷ , οὐ μὲν δή τι ἑκοῦσα , τιτυσκομένη δʼ ἐλάθοιο ·
# claude_agreement = majority
# claude_note = REVIEW: Resolved against Way's 1913 translation (theoi.com): Penthesileia, not Achilles, is the subject of κατέκτανε/ἑκοῦσα/τιτυσκομένη -- she killed her own sister Hippolyta by accident while aiming at a stag. That also explains tok16 ἐλάθοιο, which doesn't lemmatize to anything -- almost certainly a θ/φ transcription error for ἐλάφοιο (gen. sg. of ἔλαφος 'stag/deer'), genitive object of τιτυσκομένη ('aiming at a stag'). FORM kept as printed; lemma corrected. Still worth a critical-edition check, but no longer a REVIEW-blocking crux.
